      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To mitigate perceived low-frequency vibrations in an apartment, focusing on damping the structure is the most practical approach. Installing heavy, dense materials like specialized mass-loaded vinyl on walls or under flooring can help absorb vibrational energy. Strategically placing furniture, such as heavy bookshelves filled with books, against shared walls can also act as supplemental mass damping. While this won't eliminate the source, it may create a more acoustically isolated \"dead zone\" within your immediate personal space.",
